00:29:45.800 --> 00:29:47.560
So I guess he just changed his ways.

00:29:48.420 --> 00:29:50.840
Yeah. Maybe he just, like, decided drugs are cool.

00:29:50.840 --> 00:29:51.920
Maybe he changed his ways.

00:29:52.140 --> 00:29:54.340
Yeah. Maybe he changed his ways.

00:29:54.360 --> 00:29:56.580
You know what? We're not going to change our ways.

00:29:56.580 --> 00:29:57.460
We're going to do...

00:29:57.460 --> 00:29:59.200
Wait. I've got two more things.

00:29:59.600 --> 00:30:00.580
I've got a thing, too.

00:30:00.580 --> 00:30:03.220
We're going to do two things. We're going to do Joe and Sean's things.

00:30:03.480 --> 00:30:04.760
One thing. All right.

00:30:04.800 --> 00:30:06.220
He's a badass cop, okay?

00:30:06.600 --> 00:30:11.380
I'll give him that. But his walk, I'm not so certain about, like, how much that contributes to his...

00:30:11.380 --> 00:30:16.240
I mean, he's definitely comfortable and, like, he has some style to his walk, but it's more

00:30:16.240 --> 00:30:18.820
like a... It's like a dance mixed with a mall walk.

00:30:18.960 --> 00:30:20.260
Yeah. Did you guys notice this?

00:30:20.820 --> 00:30:27.940
I think that any time we play a game that has a somewhat, like, normal...

00:30:27.940 --> 00:30:32.560
Sorry. Like, we play a game that has sprites that have, like, somewhat normal proportions.

00:30:33.400 --> 00:30:35.020
The walk is always messed up.

00:30:35.220 --> 00:30:36.700
Yeah. He's race walking, though.

00:30:36.980 --> 00:30:38.900
Yeah. That's exactly what it looks like.

00:30:38.940 --> 00:30:40.980
But it goes pretty well with...

00:30:40.980 --> 00:30:41.860
This is my second thing.

00:30:41.960 --> 00:30:43.400
And I kind of mentioned it earlier.

00:30:43.940 --> 00:30:45.500
I think some of the...

00:30:45.500 --> 00:30:46.980
Like, this is some top tier music.

00:30:47.200 --> 00:30:48.740
Good. I'm glad you're bringing up the music.

00:30:48.760 --> 00:30:51.900
This is driving, like, intense action music.

00:30:52.100 --> 00:30:56.880
That's all. The only thing is that the sound effects kind of, like, clash with the music.

00:30:57.060 --> 00:30:58.100
Yeah. That's why I don't shoot.

00:30:58.100 --> 00:31:00.120
Yeah. That's why you only arrest.

00:31:00.360 --> 00:31:03.980
Right. Yeah. My thing was just...

00:31:03.980 --> 00:31:05.560
I needed to talk about the...

00:31:05.560 --> 00:31:11.920
I think the one level we didn't really touch upon is the grow house, where...

00:31:12.580 --> 00:31:17.640
There's... Each level is kind of drug-themed, or, I guess, drug-trade-adjacent-themed.

00:31:17.640 --> 00:31:23.020
And so one of them is called Sky High Nursery.

00:31:23.320 --> 00:31:28.560
And it's just where they grow and mass-produce marijuana.

00:31:28.600 --> 00:31:33.860
And you can even collect marijuana plants and turn them in as evidence.

00:31:34.940 --> 00:31:41.400
But I just think it's really funny that, like, you walk into this place, and it's got, like, peace signs everywhere.

00:31:41.840 --> 00:31:46.560
And just the plant as an icon.

00:31:46.560 --> 00:31:51.520
And you've just got these, like, really militant hippies with machine guns.

00:31:51.860 --> 00:31:53.380
It's like, wow.

00:31:54.380 --> 00:31:55.820
Yeah. There's so much going on.

00:31:55.820 --> 00:31:58.480
I'm trying to characterize these hippies, too.

00:31:58.540 --> 00:32:01.420
Like, oh, we're gonna mess up these dirty hippies right now.

00:32:01.660 --> 00:32:03.900
Like, it's literally like they're just, like...

00:32:03.900 --> 00:32:06.520
They're just hippies with, like, yeah, like, peace symbols.

00:32:06.680 --> 00:32:07.640
And they're just...

00:32:07.640 --> 00:32:09.760
They're just... You think it's like, oh, they're just stoners.

00:32:09.820 --> 00:32:11.680
And then they come out, and they all got machine guns and everything.

00:32:11.840 --> 00:32:14.500
So good. And as a kid, you're like, oh, this must be what hippies are.

00:32:17.040 --> 00:32:21.680
And now that we've covered Joe's important thoughts and Sean's most important thought,

00:32:21.680 --> 00:32:26.420
we can do the most important thing for the show, and that is the Essential Games List.

00:32:29.880 --> 00:32:31.700
NARC caught me by surprise.

00:32:32.320 --> 00:32:36.040
I feel like by now it has this reputation, but it didn't...

00:32:36.040 --> 00:32:37.700
I didn't know about this game like that.

00:32:37.800 --> 00:32:43.980
I wasn't even sure, to Sean's point, like, was it gonna be taking the anti-drug thing seriously or not?

00:32:44.180 --> 00:32:45.620
Still don't know if it actually did that.

00:32:45.780 --> 00:32:48.860
Like, it kind of aged in a way where it's funny again.

00:32:49.520 --> 00:32:53.440
But this is really just, like, a curiosity for those things.

00:32:53.620 --> 00:32:59.720
The actual gameplay, the weird controls of, you know, tap quickly to do this one thing

00:32:59.720 --> 00:33:07.400
and press to do this other thing really hurt the gameplay more than anything else about this game.

00:33:07.400 --> 00:33:12.400
And then I was comparing it to the run-and-gun games that we've had on the NES,

00:33:12.560 --> 00:33:15.000
but that's not... It's not that level.

00:33:15.000 --> 00:33:21.900
It is slower, and it's one of those to do a classic Joe line.

00:33:22.080 --> 00:33:23.800
It's one of those, you know, watch out for that bullet.

00:33:24.080 --> 00:33:28.800
Like, when you can see the bullets being shot, it's not high-flying.

00:33:28.800 --> 00:33:30.440
It's not action-packed.

00:33:30.880 --> 00:33:36.060
Body parts are exploding, sure, and you're able to arrest people.

00:33:36.060 --> 00:33:39.600
But it's not nearly as exciting as we describe on this episode.

00:33:39.600 --> 00:33:41.900
And I think that's what NARC is ultimately missing.

00:33:42.100 --> 00:33:48.460
If this was a faster-paced, hotline Miami, to Sean's point earlier, style game

00:33:48.460 --> 00:33:56.620
where things were much more intense and situational and not just walk in a straight line,

00:33:56.620 --> 00:33:59.280
I feel like I might have enjoyed this game.

00:33:59.280 --> 00:34:01.500
But that would make this an entirely different game.

00:34:01.500 --> 00:34:06.320
You know, we could go into different ways to improve the pacing or the weapon variety

00:34:07.880 --> 00:34:11.360
or, you know, even just, like, hit detection in one way or another.

00:34:11.480 --> 00:34:14.340
But I really think controls was the takeaway for me of just, like,

00:34:14.400 --> 00:34:18.920
well, they got it wrong from the start, and that only hurt everything else afterwards.

00:34:19.140 --> 00:34:20.800
So for that, it's a no for me.

00:34:20.940 --> 00:34:22.180
What about you, Sean? Yeah.

00:34:22.880 --> 00:34:26.060
The game itself is kind of hit and miss.

00:34:26.240 --> 00:34:29.000
I'm kind of hot and cold on it in terms of, like, the actual gameplay.

00:34:29.000 --> 00:34:33.540
Like I said, I think there's a lot of parts in it that just feel kind of awesome.

00:34:34.620 --> 00:34:39.900
But, like, yeah, you know, just sort of, like, ducking and jumping and shooting

00:34:40.360 --> 00:34:43.000
and blowing people up, like, that's pretty fun.

00:34:43.200 --> 00:34:47.260
The controls, once you get into any situation where it doesn't just, like,

00:34:47.280 --> 00:34:49.860
mow down the enemies, kind of get annoying.

00:34:51.360 --> 00:34:56.580
So that, it's nothing special when it comes to just, like, the base gameplay.

00:34:56.580 --> 00:35:01.280
But what I really like about this game is just how, like, this is, I think,

00:35:01.360 --> 00:35:06.740
the first game that we've played that it's, like, the cultural,

00:35:06.740 --> 00:35:09.120
the cultural context has changed.

00:35:10.440 --> 00:35:13.440
We've played a lot of games that haven't aged well in one way or another,

00:35:13.440 --> 00:35:17.040
and we have games that have aged well in one way or another.

00:35:17.040 --> 00:35:20.620
But I feel like this is the first one that just, like, it's almost,

00:35:20.720 --> 00:35:25.740
you can't even tell what it was trying to do or whether it was being sincere.

00:35:26.020 --> 00:35:30.920
It's weird that this is, like, a game that we're playing that's kind of comedy now.

00:35:31.640 --> 00:35:33.540
Maybe it wasn't trying to be that.

00:35:33.900 --> 00:35:36.780
So I just really dig the vibes.

00:35:37.340 --> 00:35:39.960
Whatever they were going for, I don't really care,

00:35:39.960 --> 00:35:42.460
because now this is what this game is about to me.

00:35:42.680 --> 00:35:48.320
It's about being the worst cop imaginable in the worst city imaginable.

00:35:48.600 --> 00:35:53.260
And so I think I'm going to remember this game for a long time.

00:35:53.440 --> 00:35:55.160
But, yeah, not an essential game.

00:35:55.300 --> 00:35:58.600
Joe? Yeah, I'll say that when you start this game at the beginning

00:35:58.600 --> 00:36:01.880
and in the first few levels even, this game is great fun.

00:36:02.020 --> 00:36:02.880
It really does.

00:36:03.040 --> 00:36:04.640
I think it's going to stick with me, too.

00:36:04.640 --> 00:36:10.720
It's just that edge that it has to it and, like, the kind of crazy action

00:36:10.720 --> 00:36:14.400
that you don't get in a lot of other games of this era makes it pretty fun.

00:36:14.560 --> 00:36:17.140
It is after a few levels, after playing for a little while,

00:36:17.280 --> 00:36:20.780
that I start to notice a lot of the problems that you guys mentioned in your votes.

00:36:21.380 --> 00:36:24.400
And they definitely weigh it down.

00:36:25.300 --> 00:36:28.420
I think this game needed more to be considered essential.

00:36:28.760 --> 00:36:30.660
But I don't know if we still do this anymore.

00:36:30.660 --> 00:36:33.380
It's been a long time. But I'd give it a play it, for sure.

00:36:33.380 --> 00:36:34.660
But definitely not essential.

00:36:34.820 --> 00:36:35.780
Yeah, definitely play it.

00:36:35.840 --> 00:36:37.140
Get that sleaze in there.

00:36:37.500 --> 00:36:41.520
I was going to say, yeah, I think I'd say play it for nothing related to the gameplay.

00:36:43.140 --> 00:36:48.420
You know? Play it to experience this wild ride and also to get a job at the DEA,

00:36:48.480 --> 00:36:49.640
if anybody's looking. Well, yeah.

00:36:49.820 --> 00:36:50.920
This is the starting point.

00:36:51.020 --> 00:36:52.760
It's the only thing you need on your resume.

00:36:53.340 --> 00:36:55.540
Yeah. If you can beat it, you have to have beaten it.

00:36:55.640 --> 00:36:57.360
Yes, of course. To work for the DEA.

00:36:57.540 --> 00:37:00.080
Think about how many other jobs require 10 years of experience

00:37:00.080 --> 00:37:01.300
before you can get a job.

00:37:01.300 --> 00:37:05.180
And this one just requires you to beat a 19-minute video game according to...

00:37:05.800 --> 00:37:09.280
19 minutes. See, NES long play has it at 19 minutes and 8 seconds.

00:37:09.500 --> 00:37:11.480
I didn't beat it in 19 minutes and 8 seconds.

00:37:11.640 --> 00:37:15.180
But I do think that these long plays are always funny because, you know,

00:37:15.240 --> 00:37:18.540
say I'm just looking at the next random NES long play that pops up.

00:37:18.700 --> 00:37:21.920
Metal Gear. That one is an hour and 22 minutes.

00:37:22.100 --> 00:37:23.980
Now, obviously, that one's a lot longer, too.

00:37:24.060 --> 00:37:26.220
I didn't beat that in an hour and 22 minutes.

00:37:26.220 --> 00:37:27.600
I didn't beat that game at all.

00:37:28.020 --> 00:37:32.320
But, you know, like, that still feels like, oh, there's a lot to this, right?

00:37:32.340 --> 00:37:35.140
That it took a perfect run of this game.

00:37:35.280 --> 00:37:38.580
It took them an hour and 22 minutes of NES time to do that.

00:37:38.960 --> 00:37:44.100
Here, 19 minutes of everything you need to see to see the entire game?

00:37:44.580 --> 00:37:45.520
That's a red flag.

00:37:45.740 --> 00:37:46.720
There's a red flag.

00:37:46.780 --> 00:37:48.260
But still awesome flag.

00:37:48.260 --> 00:37:49.660
It's an awesomely red flag.

00:38:14.520 --> 00:38:17.160
Oh, and hey, we had a lot of laughs on this episode.

00:38:17.540 --> 00:38:20.420
But I do want to talk about something serious, and that's doing drugs.

00:38:20.620 --> 00:38:21.720
It's pretty fucking awesome.

00:38:22.060 --> 00:38:23.340
Oh. Oh, okay.

00:38:23.460 --> 00:38:25.440
I mean, whatever. It's my opinion.

00:38:25.760 --> 00:38:27.520
Don't do drugs. But, you know, teach their own.
